class:: ShaderTexture
summary:: Static image texture resource for the SCShader renderer
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/Shader, Classes/ShaderServer

description::
Loads one static image into the renderer GPU process. PNG, JPEG, and PNM image decoding is provided by the maintained Rust code::image:: crate. Create it after its ShaderServer is ready, then bind it using link::Classes/Shader:: code::setTexture(\source, texture)::.

The current renderer supports one named binding, code::\source::. Decode failures report code::E_TEXTURE_LOAD:: and retain the requested resource ID with a small magenta/black placeholder. Images are limited to 4096 pixels per axis or the GPU limit if smaller. The renderer caches decoded RGBA pixels for one in-process GPU-device recovery, costing four CPU bytes per pixel in addition to GPU storage. GPU failures follow ShaderServer's separate recovery/fatal-exit policy. This is not yet a video, camera, shared-memory, FFT, or general texture-reflection API.

classmethods::

method:: new

argument:: path
Path to a readable PNG, JPEG, or PNM image.

argument:: server
Ready ShaderServer. Defaults to code::ShaderServer.default::.

method:: at

argument:: id
Texture resource ID.

returns::
The registered ShaderTexture or code::nil::.

instancemethods::

method:: free

discussion::
Releases the renderer texture resource. Free a texture only after rebinding the shader or disabling feedback; the renderer falls back to its black source texture if the active source is freed.

